  "body_markdown": "(310)-481-0111\n\nDental Implants\n\nDental Implant Surgery\n\nAll-on-4® Dental Implants\n\nHybrid Fixed Detachable Denture\n\nZirconia Fixed Bridge\n\nImplant Supported Dentures\n\nRobotic Surgery\n\nCost & Compare\n\nWhat To Expect\n\nFAQ\n\nAesthetic Dentistry\n\nCosmetic Dentistry\n\nPorcelain Veneers & Lumineers\n\nInvisalign\n\nTeeth Whitening\n\nSmile Makeover\n\nServices\n\nIV Sedation\n\nBone Grafting\n\nRidge Augmentation\n\nSinus Augmentation\n\nTooth Extractions\n\nGeneral Dentistry\n\nPeriodontics\n\nConditions We Treat\n\nMissing Teeth\n\nBone Loss\n\nFailing Dental Implants\n\nLoose Dentures\n\nPatient Center\n\nInsurance & Financing\n\nOur Facility\n\nPatient Stories\n\nBefore & After Photos\n\nWho We Are\n\nCommitment To Excellence\n\nMeet Dr. Tony Barriere\n\nMeet The Team\n\nVideo Library\n\nBlog\n\nContact Us\n\nPatient Portal\n\nNew Patients\n\nCurrent Patients\n\n\n## What Foods Can I Have After Dental Implant Surgery?\n\n\nApril 29, 2022\n\n\n#### Share This Post\n\n\nShare on facebook\n\nShare on linkedin\n\nShare on twitter\n\nShare on email\n\nIf you are experiencing tooth loss or decay, you might be interested in learning about options to remedy this issue. If so, a dentist may suggest placing dental implants in Los Angeles, CA.\n\nDental implants are a great way to get a new beautiful smile, and there are several options that offer this result in a natural looking and functioning way, that will allow you to execute daily activities with a new look and smile!\n\n\n## How Do Dental Implants Work?\n\n\nYou may be wondering about how the dental implantation process works and how your results may look. Dental implants are placed in the bone of the jaw and are then covered with a natural looking crown or tooth cap to replace any teeth that are unhealthy, crooked, or not suitable for a healthy oral environment.\n\nBefore getting dental implants placed, a dental specialist will assess the health of your jaw, mouth, and gums to make sure you are the right candidate for dental implants, as this can affect the longevity of the implants.\n\nAlthough dental implants function like natural teeth, it is important to care properly for them as they are an investment that is meant to last a lifetime. This means ensuring that they are cleaned per instructions from a dentist. Making sure to keep up with regular dental appointments to make sure things are going smoothly are one of the most important things you can do.\n\n\n## So What Can I Eat?\n\n\nYou’ll want to make sure your diet mainly consists of soft, gentle foods following dental implant surgery, including items like applesauce, avocados, baked beans, bananas, pasta, or smoothies. Avoiding any harsh, acidic, hard, spicy, or sticky foods will be in your best interests.\n\nAfter receiving your permanent restorations and fully healing from your implant surgery, you should be able to eat almost anything that you would be able to with normal teeth! Because of the way that dental implants are anchored into your mouth, they function like a natural tooth root and provide the same kind of support that a natural tooth root would provide.\n\n\n## Are You Considering Dental Implants?\n\n\nDental implants can be a great way to achieve a new look and smile in a way that is long-lasting, natural looking, and function just like natural teeth. It is important to choose a dental professional in Los Angeles, CA that understands your wants and needs regarding this restorative process, and will guide you in the right direction of a customized treatment plan.\n\nGet on the path to a new smile by contacting our doctor, Dr. Tony Barriere, in our office in Los Angeles, CA and schedule a consultation to learn more today!\n\nPrevPreviousHow Many Types Of Dental Implants And Techniques Are There?\n\nNextWhat Is Osseointegration When It Comes To Dental Implants?Next\n\n\n#### More To Explore\n\n\n\n### Are There Factors That Determine Which Type Of Dental Implant Procedure I Can Get Treated With?\n\n\nDental implants in Los Angeles, FL, are a safe and effective way to replace missing or damaged teeth. They are\n\nRead More »\n\nAugust 20, 2023\n\n\n### Does Anything Happen To My Jawbone If I Don’t Immediately Replace My Missing Teeth With Dental Implants?\n\n\nDental implants in Los Angeles, FL, are a gold standard tooth replacement option that are surgically placed in a patient’s\n\nAugust 14, 2023\n\n\n## You Are Welcome Here.\n\n\nSchedule your consultation today.\n\nCall Now\n\nFacebook Instagram Youtube Yelp Google\n\n\n#### Contact Us\n\n\nAddress:\n\n12301 Wilshire Blvd Suite 205,\n\nLos Angeles, CA 90025\n\n(310) 481-0111\n\n\n#### Hours\n\n\nMonday: 9:00am – 5:00pm\n\nTuesday: 9:00am – 5:00pm\n\nWednesday: 9:00am – 5:00pm\n\nThursday: 9:00am – 5:00pm\n\nFriday: 9:00am – 5:00pm\n\nSaturday: Closed\n\nSunday: Closed\n\n\n#### Services\n\n\n\n#### About Us\n\n\nPrivacy Policy\n\nDental Website by Progressive Dental Marketing",
